glamor: refuse softpipe as well as llvmpipe.

Without a hardware Mesa driver for the device (for example Mesa 21.3 on
virtio-gpu without virgl, or a GPU whose DRI driver is not installed), GBM
falls back to kms_swrast, which on a Mesa built without LLVM is softpipe.
glamor then renders on a software rasterizer that is slower than llvmpipe,
which glamor already refuses; the modesetting driver's shadow framebuffer
is faster. Treat softpipe like llvmpipe.

diff --git a/glamor/glamor_egl.c b/glamor/glamor_egl.c
index 5cf7014..30c5038 100644
--- a/glamor/glamor_egl.c
+++ b/glamor/glamor_egl.c
@@ -1150,13 +1150,14 @@ glamor_egl_init(ScrnInfoPtr scrn, int fd)
                    "glGetString() returned NULL, your GL is broken\n");
         goto error;
     }
-    if (strstr((const char *)renderer, "llvmpipe")) {
+    if (strstr((const char *)renderer, "llvmpipe") ||
+        strstr((const char *)renderer, "softpipe")) {
         if (scrn->confScreen->num_gpu_devices)
             xf86DrvMsg(scrn->scrnIndex, X_INFO,
-                       "Allowing glamor on llvmpipe for PRIME\n");
+                       "Allowing glamor on %s for PRIME\n", (const char *) renderer);
         else {
             xf86DrvMsg(scrn->scrnIndex, X_INFO,
-                       "Refusing to try glamor on llvmpipe\n");
+                       "Refusing to try glamor on %s\n", (const char *) renderer);
             goto error;
         }
     }
